  "notes": "Measured on 737-8200s (2024-2025); the 737-800s carry the same scheme. Some aircraft add small 'Malta Air', 'Ryanair UK' or flag marks by the registration. The small white mark low on the fin's trailing edge and the belly (no photo from below) aren't drawn. Colors are Ryanair's web brand values, not paint specs. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on two 737-800s (9H-QFO, EI-GXH) fitted to the measured 737-800 shape: the yellow line and the blue belly start at the belly about 1.3 m behind the nose tip (the lower nose is white), run lower than first drawn ahead of the wing (by about 0.1 of the half-height), and curve (smooth); the title is about 13 m long (0.335 of the fuselage, not 0.29).",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation (blue fin with a generic yellow band). The scheme itself evolved from the late-1990s blue-and-yellow; the flat harp and bigger 'RYANAIR' titles date from the 2013 logo refresh (date not confirmed from an official source)."
